      "writtenOn": "2026-02-16T00:39:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please try to avoid using phrases like \"This change ...\". Given this is the commit message of the change in question, I certainly hope that the message describes the change, and not some other change 😊\n\n\"This change introduces\" can be replaced with e.g. \"Add\":\n\n\u003e Add an optional ...\n\nBroadly, writing in the \"imperative mood\" makes for succinct commit messages.",
